The Obsolescence of the Warrant Requirement: The procedural safeguard of the Fourth Amendment—the requirement of probable cause reviewed by an impartial magistrate—is structurally incapable of regulating a continuous, ambient neuroweapon. A search is no longer a discrete event bounded by time and geography (e.g., searching a house or a phone); it becomes a permanent, omnipresent interception of biological processes.

